      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "Habitats",
          "lines": [
            "Any warm land",
            "Subterranean lairs"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Appearance",
          "lines": [
            "A 30-foot lizard that resembles a wingless red dragon. It has gray scales, a back mottled with red and brown, and a reddish underside. Hatchlings are light gray and darken with age."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Damage immunities",
          "lines": [
            "Fire"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Combat mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Claws and bite · Its regular attacks are two raking claws and a bite.",
            "Fiery cone · It can breathe fire simultaneously with its claws and bite. The cone is 15 feet long, 5 feet wide at the mouth, and 10 feet wide at the end. It deals 2–12 fire damage, halved by a successful save vs. breath weapon.",
            "Fire immunity · It is immune to fire-based attacks."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Lair mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Hunting cycle · It sleeps about half the time and leaves its lair every fortnight to hunt. It carries prey back and collects shiny objects.",
            "Eggs · A lair has a 10% chance to contain 1–4 eggs. Young lizards leave to hunt after hatching."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Table notes",
          "lines": [
            "1–4 appearing. Very rare. Solitary organization. Day activity. Carnivorous and neutral.",
            "Animal intelligence (1). Treasure B, Q (×10), S, T. Steady (11–12) morale. Magic resistance Nil.",
            "Monstrous Manual, TSR 2140, January 1994 third printing, p. 226."
          ]
        }
      ],
